{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"serverInfo":{"name":"petmcp","version":"devel"},"instructions":"PetMcp emulates the Commodore PET 3032 with an SD2PET disk drive on its IEEE-488 bus. emu_status says what runs. Integers may be written as hex strings, \"0x1000\" or \"$1000\". The tools are the methods of docs/spec/control-protocol.md."}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"cpu_disassemble","description":"Disassembles instructions as the 6502 would read them, without the side effects of reading; undocumented opcodes are marked with a star.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"Where to start."},"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many instructions, at most 1000."}},"required":["address","count"]}},{"name":"cpu_get_state","description":"The 6502's registers at the instruction boundary the PET stands at, the instruction there, and the cycle it begins in.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_pause","description":"Pauses the PET where it runs by itself: in the desktop application, which then runs it only on request. petmcp-cli runs only on request anyway.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_reset","description":"Pulls the PET's reset line: the 6502, the PIAs and the VIA reset, RAM and the video run on. With power, switches it off and on instead: RAM as at power-up, the ROMs read again.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"power":{"type":"boolean","description":"Switch off and on rather than reset; false when left out."}}}},{"name":"emu_resume","description":"Lets the PET run by itself again, where it does: in the desktop application.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_run_cycles","description":"Runs cycles of the 1 MHz clock, and stops at the next instruction boundary.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Cycles to run at least."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_frames","description":"Runs through frame boundaries, where the vertical blank begins, 60.1 a second, and stops at the next instruction boundary.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Frame boundaries to run through."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_until","description":"Runs until a condition holds at an instruction boundary: the 6502 about to run the instruction at pc, or the screen showing a text. Give one or both; with both, either stops it.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pc":{"type":"integer","description":"Stop before the instruction at this address."},"screen_contains":{"type":"string","description":"Stop when the screen, as video.screen_text reads it, shows this text on one line."},"timeout_cycles":{"type":"integer","description":"Cycles after which to give up; 20,000,000 (20 s) when left out."}}}},{"name":"emu_status","description":"The emulator's version, whether the window's own run is paused, and the PET's time: cycles of its 1 MHz clock and frames since power-up; or, when it is not running, why.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"memory_list_regions","description":"The memory regions memory.read and memory.write address, with their sizes.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"memory_read","description":"Reads bytes, without the side effects a read by the 6502 has: by default as the 6502 sees its address space, I/O registers and the bus left floating included; or from a region of memory.list_regions.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte's address in the region."},"size":{"type":"integer","description":"How many bytes, at most 65536."},"region":{"type":"string","description":"CPU when left out; RAM, VIDEO_RAM or one of the ROMs."}},"required":["address","size"]}},{"name":"memory_write","description":"Writes RAM or video RAM as a debugger does: no bus cycle is made and no device runs. The whole range is checked first, so it is written whole or not at all; in CPU addresses it must lie in RAM, $0000-$7FFF, or video RAM, $8000-$87FF.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte's address in the region."},"data_hex":{"type":"string","description":"The bytes, two hex digits each."},"region":{"type":"string","description":"CPU when left out; RAM or VIDEO_RAM."}},"required":["address","data_hex"]}},{"name":"video_screen_text","description":"The 25 lines of the screen as text, as the character set on show draws them: letters, digits and punctuation as themselves, graphics as the nearest Unicode character.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"video_screenshot","description":"The last complete picture, the 320 by 200 dots of the 40 by 25 characters, completed where the vertical blank begins: lit dots white, the rest black. Written to path as a PNG, or returned as one.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the PNG; left out, it is returned."}}}}]}}
